{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"agent_message","text":"The captured interface defines `SystemCtx` as a ReadIndex operation’s identity and `ReadyToRead` as readiness for a prior batch. That grounds a narrow obligation: a released remote request must retain its identity in the response. Normal message dispatch adds no completion barrier between overlapping reads. I’ll keep client timeout and broader progress claims outside this obligation.\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > build_obligation.py <<'PY'\nimport json\nr=json.load(open('../research.json')); q=r['candidates'][0]['question'].copy()\nsources=[dict(id='S-read-identity-contract',file='raftpb/raft.go',start_line=42,end_line=54,kind='interface_statement'),dict(id='S-update-contract',file='raftpb/raft.go',start_line=69,end_line=101,kind='interface_statement'),dict(id='S-message-dispatch',file='node.go',start_line=1274,end_line=1317,kind='code_observation'),dict(id='S-peer-bootstrap',file='internal/raft/peer.go',start_line=360,end_line=437,kind='code_observation'),dict(id='S-peer-cycle',file='internal/raft/peer.go',start_line=284,end_line=317,kind='code_observation'),dict(id='S-test-storage',file='internal/raft/logdb_test.go',start_line=23,end_line=60,kind='code_observation')]\nq['unknowns']=[]\nq['disposition']='ready_for_check'\nq['source_ids']+=['S-read-identity-contract','S-message-dispatch','S-update-contract']\nq['trigger_rationale']+=' Node.handleReceivedMessages passes ordinary messages directly to Peer.Handle, and the SystemCtx interface explicitly identifies a ReadIndex operation. The proposed oracle compares response identity against the released request, not against a deadline or assumed eventual success.'\nclaim=dict(id='C-read-context',kind='obligation',concern='implementation_semantics',description='When the leader releases an admitted forwarded ReadIndex request after quorum confirmation, the ReadIndexResp sent to its requester must carry that released request\\\\'s SystemCtx unchanged, so the requester can associate ReadyToRead with the same operation. Coalesced confirmation may raise the read index but must not replace an earlier request\\\\'s context with another request\\\\'s context.',source_ids=['S-read-identity-contract','S-read-contract','S-read-aggregation','S-read-response','S-forward-read','S-read-consumer'],scope=dict(description='Per-operation response correlation for released forwarded requests within a stable leader term and membership after a current-term entry is committed.',assumptions=['Distinct nonzero SystemCtx values identify independently admitted requests.','Requests and quorum acknowledgements originate from the actual Peer handlers in one controlled history.','Non-Byzantine members; a delayed earlier response may overlap later traffic; no crash or membership change during the selected history.'],excluded=['No requirement that unconfirmed or dropped requests succeed.','No deadline or infinite-stall claim; no end-to-end NodeHost completion or stale-read consequence.','No backend crash atomicity or snapshot-recovery property.']),pending=[],grounding=dict(source_ids=['S-read-aggregation','S-read-response','S-forward-read','S-read-consumer'],expectation_ids=['S-read-identity-contract','S-read-contract'],binding_ids=['BD-read-emit','BD-read-receive'],derivation='SystemCtx is explicitly the identity of a ReadIndex operation, and ReadyToRead identifies a prior batch. The async ReadIndex API returns a per-operation RequestState. Leader confirm retains each pending record and releases a prefix; follower receipt copies the response context into ReadyToRead, whose consumer performs an exact-key batch lookup. Therefore a response for a released record must preserve its stored identity. This is an identity-preservation duty at release, not a promise of success for all calls. The suspected implementation difference is not treated as a conflicting normative source.',applicability='Forwarded requests that are actually released by a quorum confirmation in the same authority epoch.',unresolved=[],conflicts=[],alternatives=['No obligation to immediately complete a still-pending request.','One request or local-only prefix processing can preserve identity and does not exercise the remote-prefix discrepancy.']))\ndef binding(i,mat,sym,a,b,desc):\n return dict(id=i,material_id=mat,symbol=sym,start_line=a,end_line=b,description=desc,pending=[],associations=[dict(claim_id='C-read-context',source_ids=['S-read-identity-contract',mat],rationale=desc)])\nbindings=[binding('BD-read-emit','S-read-response','handleReadIndexLeaderConfirmation',1771,1790,'Consumes released readStatus objects and encodes each remote response destination, index and context.'),binding('BD-read-receive','S-forward-read','handleFollowerReadIndexResp',1955,1963,'Copies received response identity into ReadyToRead for exact-context client consumption.')]\nm=json.load(open('../audit-spec/v1.json'))\nb=next(x for x in m['behaviors'] if x['id']=='B-read-client')\nb['unknowns']=[]\nb['important_branches'].append('Ordinary ReadIndex and ReadIndexResp messages pass node.handleReceivedMessages/handleMessage directly to Peer.Handle without waiting for earlier read completion.')\nb['source_ids']+=['S-message-dispatch','S-read-identity-contract']\n# The overview cites selected behavior source sets as required by the product contract.\nm['core_overview']['connection']['source_ids']+=['S-message-dispatch','S-read-identity-contract']\njson.dump(m,open('map-read-contract.json','w'),indent=2)\ns=dict(action='obligation',candidate_id=r['candidates'][0]['id'],rationale='Fix the sourced per-operation correlation responsibility before executing a history. The oracle will use independent requester identity and original SystemCtx; it will not infer a global liveness obligation.',question=q,sources=sources,obligation=claim,bindings=bindings,map_path='map-read-contract.json',map_changes={'B-read-client':dict(impact='clarification',source_ids=['S-message-dispatch','S-read-identity-contract'],rationale='Resolve the previously unread ordinary-message dispatch premise and make the operation identity interface explicit.',preserves='The principal Fact, its producer/consumer edges and the candidate\\\\'s remote response-correlation question are unchanged; dispatch adds no completion barrier and does not change admissible overlap.')},feedback=dict(ref_ids=[r['candidates'][0]['id'],'B-read-client','S-message-dispatch','S-read-identity-contract'],answered='Ordinary read request/response dispatch does not serialize completion across contexts. The captured identity interface and exact-context consumer establish an operation-correlation duty when pending records are released. Persistence ordering for the future driver is explicit in Update: store state/entries before sending non-replication messages.',remaining=['A controlled Peer history must observe actual admission, quorum release, emitted replies and destination ReadyToRead without injecting private pending records or fabricated acknowledgements.'],understanding='updated',rationale='The obligation concerns correspondence at a completed protocol action; it neither assumes all reads succeed nor claims finite waiting proves stalling.'))\njson.dump(s,open('submission-obligation.json','w'),indent=2)\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python build_obligation.py\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-04_11-52-07-dragonboat_raft-real-run --submission submission-obligation.json\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
